[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/588248644","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979#issuecomment-588248644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979","id":588248644,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU4ODI0ODY0NA==","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-02-19T14:06:10Z","updated_at":"2020-02-19T14:06:10Z","body":"Text of license copied below from original submission:\r\n\r\n> The WiX toolset is released under the Microsoft Reciprocal License (MS-RL). A reciprocal license is used to ensure that others who build on the effort of the WiX community give back to the WiX community. Specifically the license requires that fixes and improvements to the WiX toolset must be published using the same license.\r\n> \r\n> Sometimes the reciprocal license is incorrectly interpreted to also apply to bundles, packages, and custom actions built using the WiX toolset. The Outercurve Foundation has previously provided this statement below to clarify which now the .NET Foundation reaffirms:\r\n> \r\n> The WiX toolset (WiX) is licensed under the Microsoft Reciprocal License (MS-RL). The MS-RL governs the distribution of the software licensed under it, as well as derivative works, and incorporates the definition of a derivative work provided in U.S. copyright law. OuterCurve Foundation (and the .NET Foundation) does not view the installer packages generated by WiX as falling within the definition of a derivative work, merely because they are produced using WiX. Thus, the installer packages generated by WiX will normally fall outside the scope of the MS-RL, and any of your source code, binaries, libraries, routines or other software components that are incorporated in installer packages generated by WiX can be governed by other licensing terms.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/588248644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/592230106","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979#issuecomment-592230106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979","id":592230106,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU5MjIzMDEwNg==","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-02-27T23:28:48Z","updated_at":"2020-02-27T23:28:48Z","body":"this seems more like either a \"clarification\" of what WiX thinks MS-RL means in relation to the WiX installer packages and the meaning of \"derivative work\"  \r\n\r\nI'm not sure this rises to the level of an \"exception\" to the license terms? \r\n\r\nWould be nice to have someone from the WiX to comment or maybe @stephenrwalli has some insights, as he was involved with OuterCurve","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/592230106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/592475758","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979#issuecomment-592475758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979","id":592475758,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU5MjQ3NTc1OA==","user":{"login":"Jon-Work","id":34033471,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDMzNDcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34033471?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work","html_url":"https://github.com/Jon-Work","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jon-Work/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-02-28T11:36:22Z","updated_at":"2020-02-28T11:36:22Z","body":"It's like the \"Linux-syscall-note\" exception that is already in the SPDX list.\r\n\r\nLawyers can argue whether in legal-speak it is a \"note\", \"statement\", \"exception\", \"clarification\", or something else.  But SPDX only has a technical category called \"exceptions\" that handles things like this, so it needs to be a SPDX \"exception\".","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/592475758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/592600571","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979#issuecomment-592600571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979","id":592600571,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU5MjYwMDU3MQ==","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-02-28T16:53:04Z","updated_at":"2020-02-28T16:53:04Z","body":"@Jon-Work - do you represent WiX?\r\n\r\nwe had Linux contributors involved with the addition of the Linux-syscall-note and there was quite a bit of discussion about that.  So, discussion here is also just as appropriate.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/592600571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/604579043","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979#issuecomment-604579043","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979","id":604579043,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYwNDU3OTA0Mw==","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-03-26T17:48:34Z","updated_at":"2020-03-26T17:48:34Z","body":"@Jon-Work - oops, sorry, you already said you don't represent WiX\r\n\r\nany ideas on who we can tag for some insight on the intentions here?\r\n\r\nas for the \"lawyers can argue\" comment (which comes across a bit snarky - this is the SPDX legal team, which is made up of some lawyers who have worked very hard to make the SPDX License List a consistent, reliable and usable thing!) - yes, we have a category called \"exceptions\" and we have had long discussions as to naming, but regardless of what it's called, the concept of what goes on that part of the list is what matters, see top of https://spdx.org/licenses/exceptions-index.html - notably this:\r\n\"These exceptions grant an exception to a license condition or additional permissions beyond those granted in a license; they are not stand-alone licenses. \"\r\n\r\nthat's what I was trying to get at.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/604579043/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/625370857","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979#issuecomment-625370857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/979","id":625370857,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYyNTM3MDg1Nw==","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.